  🔄 **Auto-Renewal Setup (Important!)**

  Let's Encrypt expires every 90 days. Set up auto-renewal:

     1 │# Create renewal script
     2 │nano /opt/otk-app/renew-letsencrypt.sh

  Paste:

     1 │#!/bin/bash
     2 │set -e
     3 │
     4 │echo "[$(date)] Starting certificate renewal..."
     5 │
     6 │# Stop frontend to free port 80
     7 │cd /opt/otk-app
     8 │docker compose stop frontend
     9 │
    10 │# Renew certificate
    11 │certbot renew --quiet --deploy-hook "
    12 │  cp /etc/letsencrypt/live/otk-help.martinmeer.com/fullchain.pem /opt/otk-app/ssl/cert.pem
    13 │  cp /etc/letsencrypt/live/otk-help.martinmeer.com/privkey.pem /opt/otk-app/ssl/key.pem
    14 │  chmod 644 /opt/otk-app/ssl/cert.pem
    15 │  chmod 600 /opt/otk-app/ssl/key.pem
    16 │"
    17 │
    18 │# Restart frontend
    19 │docker compose start frontend
    20 │
    21 │echo "[$(date)] Certificate renewal complete!"

  Make executable and schedule:

     1 │chmod +x /opt/otk-app/renew-letsencrypt.sh
     2 │
     3 │# Add to crontab (runs daily at 3 AM)
     4 │sudo crontab -e
     5 │
     6 │# Add this line:
     7 │0 3 * * * /opt/otk-app/renew-letsencrypt.sh >> /var/log/letsencrypt-renew.log 2>&1

  Test renewal (dry run):

  sudo certbot renew --dry-run